title: The Paper's Campaign
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and lw_campaign_timer <= 0 and time >= 4
on-arrival: {!
Q.lw_campaign_timer = 5;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.lw_campaign_played = (Q.lw_campaign_played || 0) + 1;
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.card();
!}
frequency: 150
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs

= The Paper's Campaign

The editors of Die Rote Fahne want a campaign: one subject, on the front page every day for a month, with leaflets, meetings and posters to follow it into every district. A paper that says everything, the chief editor says, is a paper nobody remembers.

They have a pile of proposals, and room for one.

- @murders: Campaign against the unpunished murders.
- @prices: Name the profiteers.
- @frontline: Call on all workers to close ranks.
- @betrayal: Expose the social democratic leaders.
- @russia: Campaign for Soviet Russia.
- @easy_discard

@murders
subtitle: The nationalist killers and the judges who free them. Worker support grows; the right wing is furious. The Spartacist theme.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.stability += 1;
Q.repression += 2;
RG.news('Rote Fahne campaign: Germany\'s unpunished murders', 3);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 4);
!}

Every day a new name: a worker shot "while trying to escape", a deputy murdered on his doorstep, a judge who gave the killer four months. The series ends with a list of three hundred names, and a question for the Minister of Justice.

@prices
subtitle: The anger of the housewives and the unemployed, given a target. Militancy and support grow.
view-if: inflation >= 25 or year >= 1921
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.militancy += 3;
RG.news('Rote Fahne names the profiteers', 3);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 2);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 1);
!}

The paper prints the prices in the market halls next to the dividends of the companies that supply them, and the names of the wholesalers who hold back potatoes for a better price. Women cut out the lists and take them shopping.

@frontline
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] An appeal to the social democratic workers for joint action. Relations improve. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids appeals for unity with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('united_front');
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.uspd_relation += 3;
Q.worker_support += 2;
RG.news('Communists appeal to social democratic workers for joint action', 3);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 4);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', -1, -3);
!}

"Workers of every party, close ranks!" For a month the paper prints letters from social democratic workers, union branches and works councils that want joint action, and asks their leaders, every day, why not.

@betrayal
subtitle: Noske, the January days, the coalition with the bosses. The Left loves it; the social democratic workers do not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.militancy += 3;
RG.news('Rote Fahne: the record of the SPD leaders', 3);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 4);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', -1, -3);
!}

The paper reprints Noske's orders of January 1919, the photographs of the dead in Lichtenberg and the minutes of every coalition the SPD has joined since. The social democratic papers answer with the word "Moscow" in every headline.

@russia
subtitle: Solidarity with the first workers' state. Moscow is pleased, and the movement abroad takes heart.
on-arrival: {!
Q.world_revolution += 4;
Q.independence -= 2;
RG.ecci('all', 3);
RG.news('Rote Fahne: hands off Soviet Russia', 3);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 2);
!}

For a month the front page belongs to Russia: the civil war, the famine, the factories starting up again, the blockade. Meetings in every district collect money and pass resolutions, and the dockers of Hamburg read them.
